    "problem_statement": "A RISC-V SoC needs a way to declare additional memory regions that must be protected by the PMP, beyond the standard read-only ROM region, with specific read/write/execute permissions. Regions declared this way must be automatically collected at link time and programmed into the PMP entries during PMP initialization, appearing as global entries (in the lower half of the PMP slots) shared between modes. After PMP initialization, the PMP registers must contain entries whose decoded start address, end address and permissions match the declared regions, and the declared regions must be retrievable as a set of structured entries.",
